# World 1's mission cards keep the frame (SPEC 11, "Copper lists"): a new
# mission in the same world patches its colours into both copper lists (the sky,
# the floor's ground, the clouds', mountains' and land's palettes), as world 2's
# do, instead of writing the lists again (~0.9 A500 frame each: every world-1
# card dropped 4 pictures, worst 250 %). Covered in one run: the game's start
# from the title (mission 1), the cards of missions 2 and 3, world 2's load
# (mission 4) and the way back to world 1 (mission 1, its art loaded again).
# Each flight checks the plain's ground on the floor's last line, line 198 (C
# of that mission's floor: M1 DA6, M2 576, M3 CC8); the goldens are the same
# pictures the full rewrite drew.
wait-serial "AGK t0" 1000
press fire 2
wait 120
press fire 2
wait 40
press up 60
press left 60
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x11
wait 5
key 0x02
wait-serial "AGK start world=1 mission=2" 200
wait 60
press fire 2
wait 40
press up 60
press left 60
screenshot m2
expect-color m2 4 198 0x576
expect-color m2 315 198 0x576
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x11
wait 5
key 0x03
wait-serial "AGK start world=1 mission=3" 200
wait 60
press fire 2
wait 40
press up 60
press left 60
screenshot m3
expect-color m3 4 198 0xCC8
expect-color m3 315 198 0xCC8
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x11
wait 5
key 0x04
wait-serial "AGK world 2 loaded" 700
wait 60
press fire 2
wait 40
press up 60
press left 60
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x11
wait 5
key 0x01
wait-serial "AGK world 1 loaded" 400
wait 60
press fire 2
wait 40
press up 60
press left 60
screenshot m1
expect-color m1 4 198 0xDA6
expect-color m1 315 198 0xDA6
expect-serial "AGK world=1 mission=1"
expect-no-serial "ERR|missing"
expect-no-dropped-frames
expect-max-load 90
